.DS_Store

# Python bytecode. Chaque exercice se lance directement, donc __pycache__
# apparait des la premiere execution.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Virtualenvs. Several exercises create one next to themselves while working.
.venv/
venv/

# Jupyter scratch, written beside any notebook that has been opened.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Packaging artefacts of py-03-livrer/ex07. `pip install .` writes them, and
# they are rebuilt from pyproject.toml on demand.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Solutions to 42 subjects. This repository is public, and it is also the tree
# `./exo` grades, so completing one of these here would publish it. Two reasons
# not to: the school's charter forbids publishing subject solutions, and the
# commit dates of work done before enrolment are visible in the history.
#
# Only modules whose curriculum `source` names a 42 subject are listed. The
# additions built on top of them stay publishable, because they are the point
# of the showcase: c-02-moteur, c-07, c-08, c-10, c-11, c-12, cpp-05-vector-asm,
# cpp-11-moderne, and everything under cu-, tri-, inf-, par-, mes-, mth-, py-,
# l1- to l5-.
#
# To publish one of these after all, add its own `!` line below.
c-01-libft/
c-03-libft-norme/
c-04-printf/
c-05-gnl/
c-06-pushswap/
c-09-philosophers/
c-13-minishell/
cpp-00-classes/
cpp-01-allocation/
cpp-02-canonique/
cpp-03-heritage/
cpp-04-polymorphisme/
cpp-06-exceptions/
cpp-07-casts/
cpp-08-templates/
cpp-09-conteneurs/
cpp-10-stl/
sh-01-b2br/
sh-02-netpractice/
t42-*/

# Loose scratch and third-party data, kept local. The notebooks are Zero to Hero
# working copies and the dataset is Karpathy's, not this repository's work.
/bigram.ipynb
/micrograd2.ipynb
py-01-basics/ex00/Untitled.ipynb
py-01-basics/ex00/names.txt

# Les devoirs empruntes: leurs reponses ne se publient pas, par respect du
# meme principe que les sujets 42. Elles sont versionnees dans ml-systems.
rte-*/

# Exception, 2026-09-18: the Tensor Puzzles answers are published after all.
# Decided case by case, not as a new rule: srush's set is a public MIT exercise
# book, not a school subject under a charter. Only the finished notebook and the
# README that frames it go out. The upstream clone, its virtualenv and its test
# caches stay local, so nothing of srush's repository is republished here.
# `!rte-01-puzzles/` carries no slash, so it lifts the refusal at any depth, the
# way `rte-*/` imposed it. The lines below DO carry a slash, which anchors them
# to the repository root, so they have to name the phase as well.
!rte-01-puzzles/
ms-00-prepa/rte-01-puzzles/*
!ms-00-prepa/rte-01-puzzles/README.md
!ms-00-prepa/rte-01-puzzles/Tensor Puzzlers.ipynb

# Exception, 2026-09-21: chapter 2 of the route is published too. Decided case
# by case like the one above, and for the same reason: `rasbt/LLMs-from-scratch`
# is a public companion repository, not a school subject under a charter. Only
# my own answer goes out. The book's text, its corpus `the-verdict.txt`, its
# notebooks and its package stay where they are, so `ch02.py` cannot run from
# here -- `find_corpus` says so rather than guessing, and the file's docstring
# says why. Same shape as above: the bare line lifts the refusal at any depth,
# the anchored ones name the phase.
!rte-route-l1/
ms-00-prepa/rte-route-l1/*
!ms-00-prepa/rte-route-l1/ch02.py

# Exception, 2026-09-21: chapters 3 and 4 of the route follow, on the same
# ground and by the same case-by-case decision. One difference is worth
# stating: unlike `ch02.py`, these two run as they stand. Chapter 3 works on
# six toy embeddings written into the file, and chapter 4 needs only those
# plus the GPT-2 tokenizer, so neither reaches for the book's corpus. They are
# published together because `ch04.py` imports `MultiHeadAttention` from
# `ch03.py`: alone, it would not even import.
!ms-00-prepa/rte-route-l1/ch03.py
!ms-00-prepa/rte-route-l1/ch04.py
